# Longbridge OpenAPI — environment template
#
# Copy to .env and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; never commit real values.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# The SDK autoloads .env from the working directory (it imports
# godotenv/autoload), so `go run ./cmd/quote` picks it up automatically.
# For other tools, source it yourself:  set -a; . ./.env; set +a
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED — from https://open.longbridge.com/ -> User Center
# -> "Application credential" (应用凭证).
#
# If your account is SIMULATED, use the credential triple issued for that
# simulated account, not your live one. The two triples are independent.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# App Key. Not secret, but treat as private.
LONGBRIDGE_APP_KEY=your_app_key

# App Secret. SECRET. Anyone holding App Key + App Secret can sign requests.
LONGBRIDGE_APP_SECRET=your_app_secret

# Legacy Access Token. SECRET — this is what actually authorises TRADING.
# This is the "Access Token" shown in User Center, NOT an OAuth access token.
LONGBRIDGE_ACCESS_TOKEN=your_access_token

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL — accepted for backwards compatibility with older examples.
# LONGPORT_APP_KEY, LONGPORT_APP_SECRET and LONGPORT_ACCESS_TOKEN are read as
# fallbacks when the LONGBRIDGE_* names above are unset. Prefer the
# LONGBRIDGE_* spelling; the LONGPORT_* names are frozen.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LONGPORT_APP_KEY=your_app_key
# LONGPORT_APP_SECRET=your_app_secret
# LONGPORT_ACCESS_TOKEN=your_access_token

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OAUTH 2.0 — only read by cmd/auth, and only needed if you want to run the
# browser login. Every other command uses the app-key triple above; authorizing
# with OAuth does not switch them over.
#
# The client ID is issued from the same User Center page as the app key.
# LONGBRIDGE_CLIENT_ID is the variable cmd/auth reads; if it is unset, cmd/auth
# falls back to LONGBRIDGE_APP_KEY / LONGPORT_APP_KEY and labels the result as
# an assumption, because nothing in the SDK documents the two as the same
# string. Pass -client-id to skip the guess entirely.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LONGBRIDGE_CLIENT_ID=your_oauth_client_id

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SAFETY SWITCHES — demo-specific, not read by the SDK
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Dry run. DEFAULT is ON (1), which blocks every order write.
# The trade command only submits when this is 0 AND --confirm-live is passed
# AND LONGPORT_MODE=live.
LONGPORT_DRY_RUN=1

# Which account the credentials above belong to: simulated | live.
# Default is simulated. Writes additionally require mode=live, so a simulated
# account can never be traded into by accident.
# NOTE: the Go SDK has no paper-trading flag; this only records intent and
# enforces the safety gate. It cannot verify your credentials.
LONGPORT_MODE=simulated

# Watchlist dry run. DEFAULT is ON (1), which blocks every watchlist write.
# This is a SEPARATE gate from LONGPORT_DRY_RUN and is deliberately not
# influenced by LONGPORT_MODE: editing a saved symbol group is not trading, so
# requiring mode=live for it would be misleading. The watchlist command only
# applies a change when this is 0 AND --confirm is passed.
LONGPORT_WATCHLIST_DRY_RUN=1

# The four remaining gates all behave the same way and are all built from the
# same reusable config.WriteGuard helper. Each needs all THREE of its own
# conditions: this variable set to 0, the named flag on the command line, AND
# LONGPORT_MODE=live. None of them opens another, and any one alone still blocks.
#
# A value that is not 1/true/0/false is rejected at startup by EVERY command in
# the repo, not just the one that owns the switch — so a typo surfaces
# immediately instead of silently behaving as "dry run".
#
# Sharelist dry run. Blocks create/delete/add/remove/sort on the sharelists you
# own. Delete is IRREVERSIBLE: the SDK has no undelete endpoint.
#   flag: --confirm-live-sharelist
LONGPORT_SHARELIST_DRY_RUN=1

# Content dry run. Blocks publishing a topic or a reply, which is public,
# attributed to your account and unretractable — the SDK exposes no
# delete-topic method.
#   flag: --confirm-live-content
LONGPORT_CONTENT_DRY_RUN=1

# DCA dry run. Blocks creating, updating, pausing, resuming, stopping a plan and
# changing its reminder hours. A plan invests real money on a recurring schedule
# and Stop cannot be undone.
#   flag: --confirm-live-dca
LONGPORT_DCA_DRY_RUN=1

# Price-alert dry run. Blocks adding, updating and deleting price alerts.
#   flag: --confirm-live-alert
LONGPORT_ALERT_DRY_RUN=1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONFIG FILE (optional alternative to the three credentials above)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy config.example.yaml to config.yaml, or pass it explicitly:
#     go run ./cmd/quote -config ./my-config.yaml
#
# Only YAML is supported. The file is auto-detected as config.yaml, then
# config.local.yaml; -config PATH overrides that search. A -config path that
# does not end in .yaml is a hard error (exit 1) — the Longbridge SDK can also
# parse TOML and .env, but this demo does not wire that reader up, and the SDK
# cannot parse .yml at all.
#
# Environment variables always win over the file, so you can keep credentials
# in .env and non-secret settings in the YAML.
#
# The top-level key MUST be `longbridge:`. Copy the example rather than writing
# one from scratch.
#
# config.yaml, config.local.yaml, config.yml and config.toml are all in
# .gitignore; never commit a filled-in one.
#
#   longbridge:
#     app_key: your_app_key
#     app_secret: your_app_secret
#     access_token: your_access_token

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ENDPOINTS — leave unset unless you have a reason.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Access point. .com (default) or .cn for mainland China connectivity.
# .cn has no route to the US data centre, so US accounts must use .com.
# LONGPORT_REGION=cn

# Override the HTTP API base. Default: https://openapi.longbridge.com
# LONGBRIDGE_HTTP_URL=https://openapi.longbridge.com

# Override the quote websocket. Default: wss://openapi-quote.longbridge.com/v2
# LONGBRIDGE_QUOTE_URL=wss://openapi-quote.longbridge.com/v2

# Override the trade websocket. Default: wss://openapi-trade.longbridge.com/v2
# LONGBRIDGE_TRADE_URL=wss://openapi-trade.longbridge.com/v2

# Point every endpoint at Longbridge's .xyz staging hosts. This is NOT a
# simulated account — it changes the host only. Leave unset for normal use.
# LONGBRIDGE_ENV=staging

# Per-request timeout, Go duration syntax. Default 15s in this demo.
# LONGBRIDGE_HTTP_TIMEOUT=15s
# LONGBRIDGE_TIMEOUT=15s
# LONGBRIDGE_AUTH_TIMEOUT=15s

# Protocol tuning. Sensible defaults are built into the SDK; only set these
# when diagnosing connection problems.
# LONGBRIDGE_READ_QUEUE_SIZE=100
# LONGBRIDGE_WRITE_QUEUE_SIZE=100
# LONGBRIDGE_READ_BUFFER_SIZE=100
# LONGBRIDGE_MIN_GZIP_SIZE=1024

# Allow 24-hour US overnight trading. Required for overnight sessions.
# LONGPORT_ENABLE_OVERNIGHT=true

# Response language: en | zh-CN | zh-HK. Default en.
# LONGPORT_LANGUAGE=en

# SDK log level: trace | debug | info | warn | error. Unset disables SDK logs.
#
# `trace` is accepted by the variable but honoured by nothing: the SDK's own
# logger implements debug, info, warn and error only, so trace silently selects
# no level. `go run ./cmd/quote -log-level debug` routes the SDK's logging to
# stderr at the level you name and refuses anything it cannot honour.
# LONGBRIDGE_LOG_LEVEL=info

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EXTRA REQUEST HEADERS — demo-specific, one variable per header
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Any variable with this prefix becomes an HTTP header sent with every request.
# Each `_` after the prefix is read as `-` and the name is lower-cased, so:
#
#   LONGPORT_HEADER_X_TRACE_ID=abc123   ->   x-trace-id: abc123
#
# Prefer this to the -header flag for anything secret: a flag value lands in
# your shell history and in ps, and this file is gitignored. The YAML equivalent
# is a `headers:` mapping inside the `longbridge:` block (see
# config.example.yaml). Precedence: -header > these variables > the YAML file.
#
# REFUSED, from any of the three sources: x-api-key, authorization,
# x-api-signature, x-timestamp. The SDK sends those itself and applies extra
# headers afterwards, so setting one would silently replace the credential.
# LONGPORT_HEADER_X_TRACE_ID=abc123
